<title>TAIWAN: First Int'l 1st-half net up 93 pct.</title>
<headline>First Int'l 1st-half net up 93 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-08-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>January-June 1996</p>
<p>			 (in million T$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Turnover			   13,278 vs 10,223</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			 609 vs    361</p>
<p>    Net profit			    630 vs    326</p>
<p>NOTE - First International Computer Inc is Taiwan's second largest computer firm. The firm's higher net profit than pretax was because of tax refunding. The firm has set a 1996 pretax profit target of T$1.21 billion on sales of T$30 billion, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
</text>
